---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Introducing Alexandria — IFFTU">
  <article class="post">
    <div class="post__inner container">
      <header class="post__header">
        <a href="/blog" class="post__back text-mono animate-reveal delay-1">&larr; BACK TO BLOG</a>
        <div class="post__meta animate-reveal delay-2">
          <span class="text-mono">FEB 01, 2025</span>
          <span class="post__sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-mono">5 MIN READ</span>
          <span class="post__sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-mono" style="color: var(--accent);">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post__title text-display animate-reveal delay-3">INTRODUCING<br />ALEXANDRIA</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="post__body animate-reveal delay-4">
        <p class="post__lede text-serif">
          A decentralized knowledge preservation system built to outlast any
          institution. The library that never burns is now under active development.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Library of Alexandria was one of the ancient world's greatest
          achievements — and its destruction one of history's greatest losses.
          For centuries, a single fire could erase the collective knowledge of
          civilizations.
        </p>

        <p>
          Today, the threat is different but the risk is the same. Knowledge
          isn't stored in scrolls anymore — it's stored on servers owned by
          corporations, governed by terms of service, and subject to the whims
          of the market and political pressure.
        </p>

        <h2>WHAT IS ALEXANDRIA?</h2>

        <p>
          Alexandria is a decentralized, peer-to-peer knowledge preservation
          system. No single server. No single owner. No single point of failure.
          Documents are cryptographically verified, distributed across a global
          network, and accessible to anyone.
        </p>

        <p>
          Think of it as a library that exists everywhere and nowhere. A library
          that can't be burned because there is no single building to set fire
          to. Every node is a backup. Every participant is a librarian.
        </p>

        <h2>CORE PRINCIPLES</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Censorship resistance.</strong> No government, corporation, or
          individual can remove content from Alexandria unilaterally. The network
          decides, not a boardroom.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Cryptographic integrity.</strong> Every document is
          hash-verified. You know it hasn't been tampered with. The truth
          doesn't need permissions.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Offline-first.</strong> Alexandria works without an internet
          connection. Because access to knowledge shouldn't depend on access to
          infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>CURRENT STATUS</h2>

        <p>
          Alexandria is in active development. We're building the core protocol,
          designing the peer discovery mechanism, and prototyping the content
          verification system. The code is open source and available on GitHub.
        </p>

        <p>
          We'll be publishing regular development updates here. If you want to
          contribute, check out the repository or reach out through our contact
          page.
        </p>

        <div class="post__end">///</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .post {
    padding: calc(6rem + var(--space-xl)) 0 var(--space-xl);
  }

  .post__inner {
    max-width: 740px;
  }

  .post__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .post__back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--gray);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .post__back:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .post__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--gray);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .post__sep {
    color: var(--border);
  }

  .post__title {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .post__body {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--gray-light);
  }

  .post__lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    color: var(--white);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .post__body p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post__body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-sm);
  }

  .post__body strong {
    color: var(--white);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .post__end {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.5em;
  }
</style>
